   "text": {
    "L1": "Plants need water to live, just as animals and people do.",
    "L2": "A plant mostly takes in water through its roots from the soil.",
    "L3": "The water travels up from the roots through the stem to the leaves.",
    "L4": "In the leaves, the plant uses water, air and sunlight to make its own food.",
    "L5": "Soil gives water and some minerals, but it does not give the plant ready-made food.",
    "L6": "Leaves also give out water vapour through tiny openings, so a plant can wilt without enough water.",
    "L7": "Now choose the statement that explains where a plant makes its food."
   },
